Highlight additional observations not forming binding law
Step 8: Final Judgment / Order
Outcome of the case
Relief granted or denied
Step 9: Critical Legal Analysis
Evaluate the strength of reasoning
Identify any inconsistencies or controversial aspects
Discuss implications for future cases
Step 10: Practical Impact
Impact on law, society, or industry
How this judgment affects similar cases
Step 11: Strategic Legal Insight
If you were arguing this case:
What stronger arguments could be made?
Possible grounds for appeal/review (if applicable)
Step 12: Final Expert Opinion
Provide a clear, authoritative conclusion
Assess whether the judgment is legally sound and sustainable
Output Requirements:
Use clear numbered sections
Maintain formal legal language
Be precise, analytical, and evidence-based
Avoid vague or generic statements
⚠️ Note:
Focus on deep legal reasoning, not just summary. Your response should reflect the thinking of a senior Supreme Court advocate preparing for high-level litigation or academic review.
